================================================================================
VENDORED THIRD-PARTY CODE — generator/ AND generator_i4c/
================================================================================

Two directories in this repository are vendored from the same third party:

    generator/       the Phase 2 deliverable tree, vendored unmodified
    generator_i4c/   a second copy of the same upstream, carrying the i4C
                     variant's slide deck and CAD-export additions

Both descend from:

    Drift-Sense Synthetic Dataset Generator
    Author:  aayushraina21
    Source:  https://huggingface.co/spaces/aayushraina21/drift-sense-synthetic-data

The upstream supplies the DRAM/FinFET pattern synthesis, the mat/strip zone
composition, the structural-defect model and the SEM acquisition model.
CITATIONS.md §1 records the provenance of `generator/`; it does not yet mention
`generator_i4c/`, which should be added there.

Neither tree ships in the submission archive: ALLOW in
scripts/build_submission_zip.py names `generator/` explicitly and, being a
closed allowlist, excludes `generator_i4c/` by omission rather than by rule.
Both are nonetheless published here, so both need their terms stated.

*** UNRESOLVED: the upstream Space publishes no LICENSE file. Its terms are  ***
*** therefore undetermined, and the Apache-2.0 grant in LICENSE does not and ***
*** cannot extend to either copy. Redistributors should not assume rights    ***
*** over these directories. Resolving this requires either (a) written terms ***
*** from the upstream author, (b) removing the vendored trees and depending  ***
*** on them externally, or (c) reimplementing the pieces actually used.      ***

Files under either tree authored by this project rather than vendored — the
Phase 2 audit harness and the Phase 2/3 composition wrappers — are Apache-2.0
along with the rest of the repository.


================================================================================
TRAINED MODEL WEIGHTS — weights/
================================================================================

The checkpoints under `weights/` (notably `weights/driftsense.pt` and
`weights/driftsense_p3.pt`) were trained exclusively on synthetic data produced
by the generator described above. Their redistribution terms inherit whatever
that upstream tree's terms turn out to be. No fab-owned, customer-owned or
otherwise proprietary layout data was used in training; see TRAINING.md.


